WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.830
(upbeat jazz music)

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:03.000
- You look so sharp.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.120
- Thank you.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.580
- Our shoes kind of match,
like the color scheme.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:06.510
We called each each other.

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:07.830
- But you know.
- Yeah, these are new.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.090
That's the only reason why they're not.

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:10.290
Have y'all met before?

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:11.123
I don't know if y'all met.

00:00:11.123 --> 00:00:13.230
- Okay, so technically, yes.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.118
- Wait, really?

00:00:14.118 --> 00:00:14.951
(laughing)

00:00:14.951 --> 00:00:15.784
- Technically.

00:00:15.784 --> 00:00:16.617
- Ooh, I'm busted.

00:00:16.617 --> 00:00:17.450
When was that?

00:00:18.332 --> 00:00:21.896
- I was a child actor in New
York and I did your show.

00:00:21.896 --> 00:00:22.895
It was a bit or a-

00:00:22.895 --> 00:00:23.728
- [Kelly] What!?
- Sketch or something.

00:00:23.728 --> 00:00:24.561
I can't remember what it-

00:00:24.561 --> 00:00:25.560
- Trick or treating, maybe?

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:26.393
- Something like that.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:29.070
And I did your show and I
was like seven or eight.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:29.903
- Aw!

00:00:29.903 --> 00:00:30.840
- So technically, yes.
(audience applauding)

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.233
There's no way you should remember that.

00:00:32.233 --> 00:00:33.066
- You look the same.

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:35.113
You look just the same.

00:00:35.113 --> 00:00:37.050
- I remember like it was yesterday.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.240
That's amazing, at seven years old, wow.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.073
- Yeah, Yeah.

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:41.550
- Were you terrified being like that young

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:42.420
like doing stuff like this?

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:43.830
I would've been terrified.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:45.420
- I was a very serious child.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.253
- [Kelly] Oh really?

00:00:46.253 --> 00:00:47.250
- A very serious child. I was at work-

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:48.083
- [Kelly] You've always been that way?

00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:48.916
- I knew what I was doing.

00:00:48.916 --> 00:00:50.040
I was here to build my career.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.000
I was getting started where I could.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:51.833
- [Rosie] Wow!
- So, thank you

00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:52.666
for one of my first jobs.

00:00:52.666 --> 00:00:53.499
- You are welcome.

00:00:53.499 --> 00:00:54.630
- [Kelly] Wow.
(audience laughing)

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.540
But you, you both worked
with Shirley Ralph, right?

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:58.530
- Who I adore.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:00:59.363
- Yeah?

00:00:59.363 --> 00:01:00.240
- The great, the great Shirley Ralph.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.389
- [Rosie] She is something else.

00:01:01.389 --> 00:01:02.222
(audience applauding)
- [Tyler] Yeah.

00:01:02.222 --> 00:01:04.955
- [Rosie] And I got to see her
in Dream Girls on Broadway.

00:01:04.955 --> 00:01:05.788
- You did?

00:01:05.788 --> 00:01:06.630
- I did, more than once

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:07.860
because that was the best show

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.210
I've ever seen in my life.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.043
- Oh, I love that feeling.

00:01:10.043 --> 00:01:11.940
- And then she was the,

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.260
we were in the Flintstones together.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:16.080
She ran the adoption
agency that got me Bam Bam.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.360
So we've been friends for
a long time and I love her.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.940
I'm so happy she's getting
her, her rewards now.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.014
- [Tyler] Oh, so am I, so am I.

00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:24.337
- Yeah. You have the same experience?

00:01:24.337 --> 00:01:25.650
What does she, what does she mean to you?

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:28.620
- So Sheryl and I actually
go back pretty far.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:30.510
My baby brother, also a child actor,

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:32.280
did a show with her called Instant Mom,

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.540
for four years.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.390
So I met Cheryl, I think back in like 2014

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:37.560
or something like that.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.380
And she was just so great with him

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:42.000
teaching him how to you know,

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.370
cut his teeth in the multi-cam world.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.630
And she was just one

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:48.180
of those people who was a
constant in my life, at one point.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:50.100
So to now do a show with her

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.910
and to watch everyone
realize the magnitude

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:55.500
of who she's and watch her get her flowers

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:56.333
in that way-

00:01:56.333 --> 00:01:57.166
- Yeah

00:01:57.166 --> 00:01:58.110
- Has been a long time coming for me.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:00.510
I'm so happy that I could
even be a part of that.

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:01.680
- Well, so you're now in season two

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.420
of Abbot Elementary. So
what's new this year?

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:04.410
What's happening?

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:06.570
Other than finding things in closets?

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:08.130
- Well, as you can see in that scene

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:10.260
we are exploring more of the world, right?

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.720
We're going more into the
basement of the school

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.270
which is as terrifying as you think it is.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:17.160
And going outside of the school,

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:17.993
getting into Philly,

00:02:17.993 --> 00:02:19.440
understanding their personal lives.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.540
And we're really seeing,
for the first time,

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:24.210
these teachers start a school year.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.530
And then what that process is like.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.300
We picked up mid-school year, last year

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.890
and this time we wanted
to really take it slow

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.570
and show people some of the things

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:31.800
that they didn't know happened

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.270
before your kids arrive.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:34.680
- [Kelly] Which is really
relevant right now cuz

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.110
I think people really got a good grasp

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:39.240
of what it's like with Zoom school.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.500
You know, all the parents having to-

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.333
- [Tyler] Oh, yes.

00:02:41.333 --> 00:02:42.166
- Yeah, cuz people always complaining like

00:02:42.166 --> 00:02:43.230
"Oh I have to do this with my kids."

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:44.100
I'm like, "Great."

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.930
The teacher's been doing it for years,

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:47.010
with like 30 of 'em.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:47.843
- Years.
- Yeah.

00:02:47.843 --> 00:02:48.690
- You had two.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:50.460
- I still don't understand
that as a concept.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:52.680
Cuz I have, I think on set,

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.960
about 15 to 20 kids in my class

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.760
and just trying to get them all quiet

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:57.630
to start rolling.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:58.660
- That's what I'm saying.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:02:59.493
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:02:59.493 --> 00:03:01.200
- It's like herding cats.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.033
- Yeah.

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:03.870
- And then someone has to
go to the bathroom and now

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:05.310
we all have to go to the bathroom.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:07.020
But not at the same time.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:11.550
So it's like, I'm realizing
how much this job is,

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.110
for a teacher, and how much that,

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:14.340
what an undertaking that is.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.930
And to have kids that aren't your own.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:16.769
- Yeah.

00:03:16.769 --> 00:03:17.602
- You know, when people
are doing the Zoom,

00:03:17.602 --> 00:03:18.990
at least they're your
kids, you know what I mean?

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:19.920
You know them.
- Right.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:21.270
- But the teachers take it home too.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.103
- Yeah.

00:03:22.103 --> 00:03:23.100
- Yeah. I would've been a teacher

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.180
had I not done this.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.740
- [Kelly and Tyler] Really?
- For sure.

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:26.573
- [Kelly] Oh you love children-

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:27.406
- I love it.

00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:29.340
I would've wanna go in
the third grade, you know

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:31.440
the second grade, the first grade, even.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.820
And people are like, what are you crazy.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.680
The same way I always
wanted to have twins.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.397
And people who have twins go,

00:03:36.397 --> 00:03:38.700
"What are you crazy,
you don't want twins!"

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:41.820
But I felt like the more,
the better, you know?

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.530
So I have five and that's what happened.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:44.700
- [Tyler] Yeah.
(audience laughing)

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.430
- So is it true that you
have to be careful what

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:48.540
you text Quinta?

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:49.680
Like does...

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:50.880
I have to be careful what I text

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:51.840
Blake Shelton, on the Voice.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:52.673
- [Tyler] Really?

00:03:52.673 --> 00:03:54.670
- Yeah. Cause he, he
probably put it out there.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:55.650
- Okay. So great.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:56.520
We have the same situ-

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:57.594
Yeah.

00:03:57.594 --> 00:03:59.538
So, she will read me to
filth in the scripts.

00:03:59.538 --> 00:04:00.900
(laughing)

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:02.370
And like I'm reading it and I'm like,

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:04.324
we literally just talked about this,

00:04:04.324 --> 00:04:05.157
(audience laughing)

00:04:05.157 --> 00:04:07.380
like there's a line in the first episode

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.880
of this season and we were talking

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:10.230
about all the different ways, you know,

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:11.063
things could go well

00:04:11.063 --> 00:04:12.300
cause you were going into an award season

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.190
and I'm like, "I have contingency plans

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:16.140
for every possible reality."

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:17.647
And next thing I know,
it's in the script of like,

00:04:17.647 --> 00:04:19.830
"One of the best things I'm
good at is making a plan

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:21.060
for something to go bad."

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.820
So she'll like actively
pull things from life

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.143
and throw them in there.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:27.840
I really have to now just watch

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.250
cause I'm hoping like
none of like dating stuff

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.267
gets in there or anything like that.

00:04:30.267 --> 00:04:31.100
(laughing)

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.000
- I'm really hoping it makes it

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:32.907
- I'm really hoping it's not.

00:04:32.907 --> 00:04:34.860
- It feels, it feels interesting

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:36.510
cuz you're such a serious person.

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.580
It feels like a lot of
things are probably funny.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.170
- Yes. Yes there are.

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:41.580
And she's good at

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.410
like really working that into the script.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:44.760
- I love that, we're inspired.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.080
Yeah. Art is inspired by life.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:46.913
- Yes.

00:04:46.913 --> 00:04:47.850
- That's not her fault.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:49.830
So we need another commercial break y'all.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.780
But would you like to
shoot a Kush Ball is-

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:52.740
- I would love to.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:53.728
I've never

00:04:53.728 --> 00:04:54.586
- You never done it?

00:04:54.586 --> 00:04:55.590
- You what's-
(audience cheering)

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:56.447
- Wait.
- Okay.

00:04:56.447 --> 00:04:57.280
- Pull.
- All right.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.560
- Get it out of this little thing.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:04:59.393
- All right.
- There you go.

00:04:59.393 --> 00:05:00.420
Now aim it someone you like.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:01.800
- I'm so sorry.
(bowwww)

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:02.633
- There you go!

00:05:02.633 --> 00:05:04.080
- Hey, you caught it!
(audience applauding)

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:04.913
- There we go.

